  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "enter combat stance with enhanced damage and dodge",
    "skill1": "deal damage to target, creating terrain obstacles on the field",
    "skill2": "AoE damage on enemies recently affected by control",
    "skill3": "battle haste increase",
    "skill4": "enhanced combat capabilities while in combat stance",
    "skill5": "bonus damage against multiply-controlled targets"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Alsa]] enters a **combat stance** that boosts damage and dodge for the rest of the fight. Her ultimate curls into a ball, damaging nearby enemies and creating terrain obstacles that reshape paths. She punishes **recently controlled foes** with area strikes and gains Haste as the battle wears on. In stance she slams for extra hits and rolls away with a shield when pressured. Bonus damage lands on repeatedly controlled targets, rewarding teams that chain crowd control. Immune or ungrouped targets reduce her control payoff, and rolling away can leave her exposed.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Alsa]] threatens with **Combat Stance** dodge, terrain pillars, and boulder attacks against recently controlled foes. Race with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]] before obstacles funnel your formation; she is unaffected while curling into a ball, so do not bank on interrupting that cast. When she rolls out of position, use lasting coverage like [[Shemira]] or [[Frieren]] instead of a single-target pin. Keep her control chains from landing with the opening protection of [[Callan]], then finish her before Haste and terrain pressure compound."
}
